# macos
.DS_Store

# Phantom "name 2.ext" twins. Something on this machine intermittently preserves a
# file's previous content under a macOS-style " 2" name when the original is unlinked
# and rewritten shortly after — seen in node_modules (during an install), in .next
# (between two builds), and in src/ across a branch switch that deleted and restored
# the same files. It is not a sync client: iCloud Desktop & Documents is off, Google
# Drive mirrors nothing, and there is no endpoint agent. The culprit is unidentified
# and it does not reproduce on demand.
#
# Ignored so that `git add -A` can never commit one. A duplicate `.ts`/`.tsx` is a
# duplicate *module*, which breaks `npm run typecheck` for everybody — so the loud
# signal stays typecheck, not `git status`. Clear them with:
#   find . -name "* [0-9].*" -not -path "./node_modules/*" -not -path "./.git/*" -delete
* [0-9].*

# Wizard scratch: captured secrets and hand-check results. Never committed.
.wizard/

# Claude Code project settings — local tooling config, not project code.
# Narrow on purpose: .claude/skills/ and .claude/agents/ stay trackable.
.claude/settings.json
